    .contact-meta {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      justify-content: center;
      gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    .contact-meta a {
      color: var(--teal-deep);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .contact-meta a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .calendly-shell {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--foam);
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    .calendly-inline-widget { min-width: 320px; height: 630px; }

    .footer {
      padding: 1.5rem 0 1.65rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: var(--paper);
    }
    .footer-inner {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 0.85rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .footer-brand {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .footer-brand img {
      height: 1.55rem;
      width: auto;
      display: block;
    }
    .footer-tag {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      flex: 1 1 14rem;
      text-align: center;
    }
    .footer-year {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
    @media (max-width: 700px) {
      .footer-inner { flex-direction: column; text-align: center; }
      .footer-tag { text-align: center; }
    }

    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
      html { scroll-behavior: auto; }
      .hero-copy { opacity: 1; transform: none; transition: none; }
      .hero-media, .band-media { transform: none !important; will-change: auto; }
      .episode-thumb img { transition: none; }
      .story-track { animation: none; }
      .story-marquee { overflow-x: auto; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <!--
    THESIS: Magazine-cover coaching home — photo + serif voice first; refuse Bootstrap hero + card stack.
    OWN-WORLD: Source Serif 4 display + Source Sans 3 UI; teal/sage/foam; Jo photography as plane.
    STORY: Meet Jo → pick an entry (1:1 / StudentOpus / listen) → proof → book.
    FIRST VIEWPORT: Full-bleed portrait, serif headline with italic stress, tracked lede, one text link.
    FORM: Jillian Bremer craft bar (canon match) + Kortney offering rhythm, distilled.
    FINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md
  -->
  <header class="nav" id="site-nav">
    <div class="wrap nav-inner">
      <a class="nav-brand" href="#top" aria-label="MindfulOpus home">
        <img src="/assets/images/logos/wordmark-duo.png" alt="MindfulOpus" />
      </a>
      <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="nav-links" id="nav-toggle">☰</button>
      <ul class="nav-links" id="nav-links">
        <li><a href="#about">About</a></li>
        <li><a href="#offerings">Work</a></li>
        <li><a href="#studentopus">Student<span class="name-opus">Opus</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#podcast">Podcast</a></li>
        <li><a href="#newsletter">Newsletter</a></li>
        <li><a class="nav-cta" href="#contact">Work with me</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero" id="hero" aria-label="MindfulOpus">
      <div class="hero-media" data-parallax aria-hidden="true">
        <img src="/assets/images/jpz-counter.jpg" alt="" />
        <div class="hero-veil"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <h1>Drop the <em>grind</em>. Build a kinder <em>practice</em>.</h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">Performance &amp; well-being coaching for classical musicians</p>
        <a class="hero-link" href="#offerings">See how I work</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about reveal" id="about">
      <div class="wrap about-grid">
        <figure class="about-photo anim anim-d1">
          <img src="/assets/images/jpz-standing.jpg" alt="Jo Zakany" />
        </figure>
        <div class="about-copy">
          <p class="about-hello anim anim-d2">Hi — I’m Jo</p>
          <h2 class="anim anim-d3">Joanna P. Zakany</h2>
          <p class="anim anim-d4">
            Violist with The Cleveland Orchestra. Certified yoga instructor (RYT-200).
            Health and well-being coach (DHWCT) through Duke Integrative Medicine.
          </p>
          <p class="anim anim-d5">
            I created
            <img class="brand-inline" src="/assets/images/logos/wordmark-duo.png" alt="MindfulOpus" />
            as a way to help fellow musicians, artists, and creatives find more balance in their lives —
            born out of my own journey recovering from burnout, and built on mental skills,
            body awareness, and a kinder relationship with the work.
          </p>
          <p class="anim anim-d6">
            I dove deeper into the science and psychology behind mindfulness in my coaching certification,
            and it’s the combination of all these offerings that I bring into my work with clients.
            I want to be of service to anyone who considers their work to be in the artistic or creative field.
          </p>
          <p class="anim anim-d7">
            If this is you, I offer an alternative to toxic grind culture — a kinder process in your work
            that leads to better results, so you can live a more balanced and thriving life.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="photo-strip reveal" aria-hidden="true">
      <figure data-parallax-deep><img src="/assets/images/jpz-computer.jpg" alt="" /></figure>
      <figure data-parallax-deep><img src="/assets/images/jpz-standing.jpg" alt="" /></figure>
      <figure data-parallax-deep><img src="/assets/images/jpz-bench.jpg" alt="" /></figure>
    </div>
<section class="mission reveal" aria-label="Mission">
      <div class="wrap">
        <blockquote class="anim">“An alternative to toxic grind culture — a kinder process in your work that leads to better results, so you can live a more balanced and thriving life.”</blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

        <section class="work reveal" id="offerings">
      <div class="wrap work-grid">
        <figure class="work-photo anim anim-d1">
          <img src="/assets/images/jpz-bench.jpg" alt="" />
        </figure>
        <div class="work-copy">
          <h2 class="section-title anim anim-d2">How I work</h2>
          <p class="section-lede anim anim-d3">1:1 coaching for musicians who want better results without the toxic grind.</p>
          <p class="anim anim-d4">
            I work one-on-one with clients (in person or over Zoom) to empower you through the process of coaching.
            Coaching is a partnership: I provide the strategies and thought work, while you provide the direction
            and goals we set. Together, we explore what’s getting in the way — and what supports a kinder,
            smarter path to the work you care about.
          </p>
          <p class="anim anim-d5">
            Sessions are fully customizable and can include mindset training, performance coaching,
            time-management, decision-making, and well-being practices — plus yoga, meditation, and breathwork
            when they serve the work.
          </p>
          <h3 class="work-sub anim anim-d6">What clients often take with them</h3>
          <ul class="work-list anim anim-d7">
            <li>Self-acceptance and self-compassion as tools for better results</li>
            <li>Stress management from both a mental and physical approach</li>
            <li>Less performance-related anxiety; more resilient audition prep</li>
            <li>Mindful practicing tips, posture, and stronger mind/body connection</li>
            <li>Clearer navigation through burnout and life transitions</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="offer-go anim anim-d7" href="#contact">Book a consultation<span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="studentopus-band reveal" id="studentopus">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div>
          <h2 class="anim anim-d1">Student<span class="name-opus">Opus</span></h2>
